# Architecture

## Runtime model

- **Next.js 16 App Router, exported as a fully static site** (`next.config.ts` →
  `output: "export"`, `trailingSlash: true`, `images.unoptimized: true`). The build
  emits plain HTML/CSS/JS to `out/`.
- **No Node server at runtime.** No API routes, no middleware, no Server Actions,
  no ISR. Anything that looks dynamic is either client-side JS or a build-time render.
- Hosted on **Cloudflare Pages** (static assets). This was a deliberate move away
  from an earlier OpenNext/Workers setup — see `docs/decisions.md`.

## The one piece of server code

`functions/api/paystack-verify.js` — a **Cloudflare Pages Function** that verifies
a Paystack transaction server-side using `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` (env var, never
committed). This is the ONLY server-side code in the project. See [api](api.mdc).

## Routing & i18n

- Locale-prefixed routes: `src/app/[locale]/...`. Locales: `en, fr, pt, sw, ar`
  (`ar` is RTL). Config in `src/i18n/config.ts`.
- `params` is a **Promise** in Next 16 — always `await` it. (A past bug silently
  forced English because the homepage read `params.locale` synchronously.)
- Per-page copy lives in `src/i18n/pages/*.ts` (e.g. `booksCopy`, `mediaCopy`),
  keyed by locale. Long-tail content (book descriptions, video titles, AI replies)
  intentionally stays English.

## Data layer

- **There is no database.** All content is static TypeScript in `src/data/*.ts`
  (`books.ts`, `events.ts`, etc.). See [database](database.mdc).
- `/admin/*` renders these static files read-only and has **no auth** (known gap,
  see `docs/decisions.md`).

## Key directories

```
src/app/[locale]/   routes (pages)
src/components/      sections/, layout/, forms/, ui/, admin/, start-here/
src/data/            static content (the "database")
src/i18n/            locale config + per-page copy modules
src/lib/             shared helpers (cn, formatDate, …)
functions/api/       Cloudflare Pages Functions (server code)
public/              images, video, fonts
```
